{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519218-was-the-extralegal-division-wasted-potential","id":1519218,"title":"Was the Extralegal Division wasted potential?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-30T20:18:21-07:00","id":1519218,"title":"Was the Extralegal Division wasted potential?","content":"The Extralegal Division, an organization within the Enforcer methodology, is primarily tasked with dealing with organized crime. Members of this division often serve as advisors to the leaders of criminal organizations and some even run their own criminal enterprises.<br /> <br /> In the revised syndicate convention book, there were hints that those within the Extralegal Division desired it to become its own Methodology, and possibly even evolve into its own Convention. The book also introduced The Understanding, a syndicate organization similar to the UN but focused on organized crime. The Understanding could have played a significant role in the potential transformation of the Extralegal Division into a standalone methodology and eventually a fully-fledged Convention.<br /> <br /> However, in Technocracy Reloaded, it seems that all the foreshadowing and potential development for the Extralegal Division were either forgotten or retconned. It's understandable since the World of Darkness (WoD) setting seems to have underwent changes around the mid-2010s, leading to a new direction in the narrative. Despite this, I find it disappointing that the intriguing possibilities for the Extralegal Division were not explored further. Incorporating these developments could have enriched the overall metaplot and added depth to the setting.<br /> <br /> In conclusion, the Extralegal Division's potential as a separate Methodology or Convention appears to have been unrealized in the current WoD narrative, and this missed opportunity is regrettable, given the interesting prospects it could have offered.<br /> <br /> What do you think?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> PS: Chat GPT is way better than Grammarly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 07-31-2023, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}